----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW & CORE CONCEPTS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pacino's Inventory Management System is designed for scalable, multi-branch restaurant
operations. It provides:
  • Multi-branch stock isolation (each branch has independent quantities & thresholds).
  • Raw Material to Prepared Item yield conversion math (e.g. 7 kg raw = 50 pcs prepared).
  • Supplier / Vendor attribution and purchase traceability.
  • Inter-branch stock distribution from Central Kitchen / Mother Branch to sub-branches.
  • Strict pre-order stock validation (blocks orders if ingredients are insufficient).
  • Automated, idempotent stock deduction upon order completion / delivery.

KEY TERMINOLOGY & ENTITIES:
  1. Raw Material (type = "raw_material"):
     Unprocessed ingredients bought in bulk from wholesale vendors.
     Examples: Minced Beef (in kg), Fresh Milk (in liters), Flour (in kg), Tomatoes (in kg).

  2. Prepared Item (type = "prepared"):
     Kitchen-prepped, portioned, or cooked items derived from raw materials.
     Examples: Burger Patties 4oz (in pcs), Pizza Dough (in pcs), Sauce Portions (in pcs).

  3. Yield Conversion Ratio (Formula):
     The exact mathematical ratio converting raw units to prepared units.
     Example: pack_size = 7.0 kg Raw Beef  ===>  yield_qty = 50 pcs Burger Patties.

  4. Mother Branch (Central Kitchen / HQ):
     Branch #1 where bulk purchases are stocked, prepped into batches, and distributed.

  5. Sub-Branches (Branch Isolation):
     Locations like Manchester (Branch #2) and Birmingham (Branch #3). They receive stock
     transfers from HQ or directly purchase from local suppliers. Orders placed at a branch
     deduct stock ONLY from that branch.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. DATABASE ARCHITECTURE & ENTITY RELATIONSHIPS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [suppliers]
    • id, branch_id, name, phone, email, address
       │
       │ (1 to N)
       ▼
  [inventory_items]
    • id                      : Primary Key
    • branch_id               : Foreign Key -> branches.id
    • category_id             : Foreign Key -> inventory_categories.id
    • type                    : enum('raw_material', 'prepared')
    • name, sku               : e.g. "Minced Beef", "RM-BEEF-001"
    • quantity                : Current on-hand stock (decimal 10,2)
    • minimum_stock           : Alert threshold limit (decimal 10,2)
    • unit                    : 'kg', 'pcs', 'liters', 'packs', 'bottles'
    • purchase_price          : Cost price per unit (£)
    • selling_price           : Customer price if sold directly (£)
    • status                  : 'in_stock', 'low_stock', 'out_of_stock'
    • made_from_item_id       : Foreign Key -> self.id (points to raw item)
    • pack_size, pack_unit    : e.g. 7.00, 'kg'
    • yield_qty, yield_unit   : e.g. 50.00, 'pcs'
       │
       ├─────────────────────────────────────────┐
       ▼ (1 to N)                                ▼ (1 to N)
  [inventory_transactions]                  [stock_conversions]
    • id                                      • id
    • inventory_item_id                       • branch_id
    • supplier_id (nullable)                  • inventory_item_id (Raw FK)
    • transaction_type:                       • converted_item_id (Prep FK)
        - 'purchase' (Vendor Delivery)        • quantity (Raw Consumed)
        - 'sale'     (Order Deduction)        • created_by (User FK)
        - 'waste'    (Spoilage/Damaged)
        - 'adjustment' (Audit Reconcile)
        - 'transfer_in' / 'transfer_out'
        - 'conversion_in' / 'conversion_out'
    • quantity (decimal 10,2)
    • notes, created_by


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. COMPLETE STEP-BY-STEP BUSINESS WORKFLOWS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WORKFLOW A: Category & Raw Material Setup
-----------------------------------------
1. Create Category:
   POST /api/v1/inventory-categories
   Body:
   {
       "branch_id": 1,
       "name": "Raw Meat & Poultry",
       "description": "Uncooked fresh meats"
   }

2. Create Raw Material Item:
   POST /api/v1/inventory-items
   Body:
   {
       "branch_id": 1,
       "category_id": 1,
       "type": "raw_material",
       "name": "Minced Beef (80/20)",
       "sku": "RM-BEEF-001",
       "quantity": 100.0,
       "unit": "kg",
       "purchase_price": 4.50,
       "minimum_stock": 15.0,
       "description": "Fresh raw minced beef"
   }


WORKFLOW B: Prepared Item Setup (With Conversion Formula)
---------------------------------------------------------
Create a prepared item and link it to the raw material:
   POST /api/v1/inventory-items
   Body:
   {
       "branch_id": 1,
       "category_id": 1,
       "type": "prepared",
       "name": "Burger Patties (4oz)",
       "sku": "PR-PATTY-001",
       "made_from_item_id": 1,
       "pack_size": 7.0,
       "pack_unit": "kg",
       "yield_qty": 50.0,
       "yield_unit": "pcs",
       "quantity": 0.0,
       "unit": "pcs",
       "purchase_price": 1.20,
       "selling_price": 2.50,
       "minimum_stock": 40.0,
       "description": "4oz patties prepped in kitchen"
   }
   Formula Meaning: Every 7 kg of raw beef yields exactly 50 patties.


WORKFLOW C: Supplier Onboarding & Stock Purchases
-------------------------------------------------
1. Register Wholesale Supplier:
   POST /api/v1/suppliers
   Body:
   {
       "branch_id": 1,
       "name": "Smithfield Meat Wholesalers",
       "phone": "+44 20 7946 0991",
       "email": "orders@smithfieldmeats.co.uk",
       "address": "42 Smithfield Market, London EC1A 9LQ"
   }

2. Record Raw Stock Purchase:
   POST /api/v1/inventory-transactions
   Body:
   {
       "inventory_item_id": 1,
       "supplier_id": 1,
       "transaction_type": "purchase",
       "quantity": 70.0,
       "notes": "Weekly Bulk Meat Delivery Invoice #INV-9021"
   }
   Result: Minced Beef stock in Branch #1 increases by +70.0 kg. Supplier #1 is logged.


WORKFLOW D: Raw-to-Prepared Stock Conversion
--------------------------------------------
1. Live Preview Yield (Read-Only):
   POST /api/v1/stock-conversions/calculate
   Body:
   {
       "inventory_item_id": 1,
       "converted_item_id": 2,
       "quantity": 14.0
   }
   Response Preview: 14 kg raw beef ===> 100 pcs prepared patties.

2. Execute Atomic Conversion:
   POST /api/v1/stock-conversions/convert
   Body:
   {
       "prepared_item_id": 2,
       "packs": 2.0
   }
   Database Actions (Inside 1 Atomic Transaction):
     • Raw Beef stock: -14.0 kg  (conversion_out log created)
     • Burger Patties stock: +100.0 pcs (conversion_in log created)


WORKFLOW E: Inter-Branch Stock Distribution
-------------------------------------------
Send prepared stock from Central London (HQ) to Manchester (Branch #2):
   POST /api/v1/inventory-items/2/distribute
   Body:
   {
       "branch_id": 2,
       "quantity": 40.0
   }
   Database Actions:
     • Deducts 40 pcs from Central London (Branch #1).
     • Increments / Creates Burger Patties in Manchester (Branch #2) by +40 pcs.
     • Logs transfer_out on Branch #1 and transfer_in on Branch #2.


WORKFLOW F: Bill of Materials (BOM) & Menu Item Recipes
-------------------------------------------------------
Link selling menu items to inventory items:
   POST /api/v1/recipes
   Body:
   {
       "name": "Pacino's Double Cheeseburger",
       "branch_id": 1,
       "menu_item_id": 10,
       "ingredients": [
           {
               "inventory_item_id": 2,
               "quantity": 2.0,
               "unit": "pcs"
           }
       ]
   }


WORKFLOW G: Pre-Order Stock Validation & Blocking
-------------------------------------------------
When an order is submitted via Online Cart or POS Checkout:
   1. OrderController@store / POSController@checkout calls InventoryStockService.
   2. Verifies if the requested branch has enough on-hand stock for each ingredient.
   3. If insufficient stock:
      Aborts immediately and returns HTTP 422:
      "Insufficient stock for Burger Patties in this branch (Available: 1, Required: 2)."
      No order record is created.


WORKFLOW H: Automated Order Stock Deduction & Idempotency
---------------------------------------------------------
When an order transitions to "order_status: completed" or "delivery_status: delivered":
   1. System calls InventoryStockService::deductStockForOrder($order).
   2. Idempotency Check: Checks if a 'sale' transaction for this Order # already exists.
      If it exists, deduction is skipped (prevents double deductions on multi-status changes).
   3. Deducts ingredient quantities atomically using DB row locks (lockForUpdate).
   4. Writes inventory_transactions record:
      transaction_type = 'sale', notes = "Order #PAC-1001 (Double Cheeseburger x1)".


WORKFLOW I: Manual Audits, Adjustments & Kitchen Waste
------------------------------------------------------
1. Physical Audit Correction (+Add or -Deduct):
   POST /api/v1/inventory-transactions
   Body:
   {
       "inventory_item_id": 2,
       "transaction_type": "adjustment",
       "adjustment_type": "add",
       "quantity": 5.0,
       "notes": "Weekly physical audit count correction"
   }

2. Log Kitchen Spoilage / Waste:
   POST /api/v1/inventory-transactions
   Body:
   {
       "inventory_item_id": 2,
       "transaction_type": "waste",
       "quantity": 2.0,
       "notes": "Dropped on prep floor during lunch rush"
   }


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. COMPLETE API REFERENCE TABLE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

METHOD  ENDPOINT                                DESCRIPTION
------  --------------------------------------  ---------------------------------------
POST    /api/v1/auth/login                      Login and receive Sanctum Bearer Token
GET     /api/v1/inventory-categories            List inventory categories for branch
POST    /api/v1/inventory-categories            Create new inventory category
GET     /api/v1/inventory-items                 List items (filter by branch, type, status)
POST    /api/v1/inventory-items                 Create raw material or prepared item
GET     /api/v1/inventory-items/summary         KPI cards (total, low stock, valuation)
GET     /api/v1/inventory-items/analytics       Turnover ratio, consumption, top items
GET     /api/v1/inventory-items/export          Stream filtered inventory to CSV
POST    /api/v1/inventory-items/{id}/distribute Inter-branch stock transfer
POST    /api/v1/stock-conversions/calculate     Live preview yield math before convert
POST    /api/v1/stock-conversions/convert       Execute atomic raw-to-prepared conversion
GET     /api/v1/stock-conversions               List conversion audit logs
GET     /api/v1/inventory-transactions          List transaction history & audit trail
POST    /api/v1/inventory-transactions          Record purchase, adjustment, or waste
GET     /api/v1/suppliers                       List approved wholesale vendors
POST    /api/v1/suppliers                       Register new wholesale vendor
GET     /api/v1/recipes                         List BOM recipes
POST    /api/v1/recipes                         Create menu item recipe with ingredients


